
# ======================================================================
#
# Format         : <type>(<scope>): <subject>
# Body (optional): <detailed explanation>
#
# ======================================================================
#
# Type:
# |-> feat     - A new feature, config or tool added for the first time.
# |-> fix      - A bug fix, correcting a broken or misbehaving config.
# |-> chore    - Routine tasks, updates and tweaks.
# |-> docs     - Documentation-only changes.
# |-> style    - Aesthetic only: formatting, fonts, colors, borders etc.
# |-> refactor - Restructuring without changing behavior.
# |-> revert   - Reverts a previous commit.
#
# Scope:
# |-> The part of the codebase affected.
# |-> flake, nixos, home, git, neovim, yazi, niri, waybar etc.
#
# Subject:
# |-> Concise, imperative mood (e.g., "add", "fix", "update")
# |-> Keep it under 50 characters.
#
# Body:
# |-> Provide a detailed explanation of the change.
# |-> Explain *what* was changed and *why* it was changed, not *how*.
# |-> Wrap lines at 72 characters for readability in `git log`.
#
# ======================================================================
